---
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import { CORE_REPO, LICENSE_NAME, WEBSITE_REPO, specs } from '../data/facts';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Contribute"
  description="How to report problems, give feedback and contribute to RoboLang and to this website, and how the project is licensed."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Contribute</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      RoboLang is an early open-source project. Trying the tools and telling us what you found is a
      real contribution.
    </p>

    <h2>Where things live</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Repository</th><th scope="col">Contains</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row"><a href={CORE_REPO}>rokorobot/RoboLang</a></th>
            <td>
              The language specification, the grammar, the IR schema, the Python implementation and
              its tests.
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row"><a href={WEBSITE_REPO}>rokorobot/RoboLang-website</a></th>
            <td>This website.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Report a problem or give feedback</h2>
    <p>
      Open an issue in the <a href={`${CORE_REPO}/issues`}>core repository's issue tracker</a> for
      anything about the language or the tools. Useful reports include:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>A task file that is accepted but should not be, or rejected but should not be.</li>
      <li>A diagnostic message that is unclear or points at the wrong place.</li>
      <li>Something you wanted to express in a task and could not.</li>
      <li>Something a consumer of the JSON IR needs that is missing.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Please include the <code>.rob</code> file, the command you ran, the full output and the result of
      <code>robolang --version</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      For a mistake on this website, open an issue in the
      <a href={`${WEBSITE_REPO}/issues`}>website repository</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Work on the code</h2>
    <p>From a clone of the core repository:</p>
    <CodeBlock lang="bash" code="python -m pip install -r requirements-dev.txt" />
    <CodeBlock lang="bash" code="python -m pytest -q" />
    <CodeBlock lang="bash" code="python -m ruff check ." />
    <p>
      Before you start on a larger change, open an issue to discuss it. The
      <a href={specs.language}>language specification</a> and the
      <a href={specs.developmentPlan}>development plan</a> describe the current design and scope.
      Changes to the language begin with the specification.
    </p>
    <div class="note">
      <p>
        <strong>Scope.</strong> Contributions that add task execution, ROS 2 control or hardware support
        to the installed package are outside the current scope. Those areas are planned as later
        stages; see <a href="/roadmap/">Vision &amp; Roadmap</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>License</h2>
    <p>
      RoboLang and this website are licensed under the
      <a href={specs.license}>{LICENSE_NAME} license</a>. The software is provided without warranty.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
